<title>HUNGARY: MOTOR RACING-RESULT OF HUNGARIAN GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-RESULT OF HUNGARIAN GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of Sunday's Hungarian</p>
<p>Grand Prix motor race (Race distance 77 laps (305.536 kms).</p>
<p>1. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada) Willams. Winning time of one</p>
<p>hour, 45 minutes and 47.149 seconds.</p>
<p>2. Damon Hill (Britain) Arrows, 9.079 seconds behind.</p>
<p>3. Johny Herbert (Britain) Sauber 20.445</p>
<p>4. Michael Schumacher (Germany) Ferrari 30.501</p>
<p>5. Ralf Schumacher (Germany) Jordan 30.715</p>
<p>6. Shinji Nakano (Japan) Prost 41.512</p>
<p>7. Jarno Trulli (Italy) Prost 1:15.552</p>
<p>8. Gerhard Berger (Austria) Benetton 1:16.409</p>
<p>9. Eddie Irvine (Britain) Ferrari one lap</p>
<p>10. Ukyo Kataya (Japan) Minardi one lap</p>
<p>11. Jean Alesi (France) Benetton one lap</p>
<p>12. Tarso Marques (Brazil) Minardi two laps</p>
<p>13. Mika Salo (Finland) Tyrrell two laps</p>
<p>Not classified (did not finish)</p>
<p>David Coulthard (Britain) McLaren 65 laps completed</p>
<p>Jos Verstappen (Netherlands) Tyrrell 61</p>
<p>Pedro Diniz (Brazil) Arrows 53</p>
<p>Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy) Jordan 42</p>
<p>Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) Williams 29</p>
<p>Rubens Barrichello (Brazil) Stewart 29</p>
<p>Mika Hakkinen (Finland) McLaren 12</p>
<p>Gianni Morbidelli (Italy) Sauber 7</p>
<p>Jan Magnussen (Denmark) Stewart 5</p>
<p>Fastet lap: Frentzen 1:18.372 (182.269 kph)</p>
</text>
